Z||000000||fieroX||12-07-2001||12:24 AM||||I recently got a V6 tach for my car (ive been using a 4 cylinder tach on my 2.8 for 9 months now) and I think my TCC is broken or something, because I dont think my lockup is kicking in.  At 50 mph I run about 2600 rpm, at 60 I run 3000 rpm and at 70 I run 3500 rpm.  Is this normal?  Just seems high to me.  How can you tell if the lockup is working?  thanks<P>------------------<BR><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">     <P>http://www.fieroX.com<BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||rodmcneill||12-07-2001||12:30 AM||||The TCC will not engage till speed is above 33-35 mph in drive. If you look at tach. at around this speed you will see rpms drop about 250-300 rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||12-07-2001||12:47 AM||||I run ~ 2600rpm at 100 kph, around 2900 at 115. Easiest way to check TqCLU, is to push the gas a little while cruising. Not hard, just a bit. The motor SHOULD lug ever so slightly. If it the TCLU is not working, the engine freewheels a little, 'cos the converter is giving it a little slack.||||reg||7
Z||000003||pHoOl||12-07-2001||01:15 AM||||Yep, those numbers are about what i get<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroX||12-07-2001||01:19 AM||||Ok im not going to mess with it then.  Im pulling it in a few weeks anyway.  thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||12-07-2001||02:09 AM||||Another way to check it is get up to about forty MPH and hold steady. lighty tap the brake pedal and watch the tach needle if it is working the tach will rise and then come back down.||||reg||1
